{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgC2njgJ8R5DcQG8Bnji9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Opening a workspace with props:** `launchWorkspace2(workspaceName, workspaceProps, windowProps, groupProps)` is the entry point. Each props argument defaults to `null`, and omitting window or group props means the caller doesn't care what those are. The function throws if the workspace isn't registered to a window, or the window isn't registered to a group. `ActionMenuButton` calls it as `launchWorkspace2(workspaceName, workspaceProps, windowProps)` ([openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/action-menu2/action-menu-button2.component.tsx:97](openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/action-menu2/action-menu-button2.component.tsx)).\n\n**Conflicting group:** `launchWorkspaceGroup2` is a no-op if the same group is open with compatible props. Otherwise it prompts, and on confirm it clears all windows and opens the new group. `launchWorkspace2` checks the group first. If the group name differs or the props are incompatible, it prompts, and on confirm it replaces the group and all its windows with one window holding the new workspace.\n\n**Conflicting window:** if the window is open with incompatible window props, it prompts, then replaces that window with a new one holding only the requested workspace. If the window is open and the workspace is already open with compatible props, it restores the window and does not prompt.\n\n**Conflicting workspace:** if the workspace is open with incompatible props, it prompts and then replaces the window with one holding only the requested workspace. The prompt is scoped to workspaces up to the target.\n\n**Compatibility rule:** two prop sets are compatible if either is nullish or they are shallow-equal.\n\n**Prompt:** `promptForClosingWorkspaces` collects workspaces with unsaved changes and shows a modal. If none exist, it resolves `true` without showing anything.\n\n**Discrepancy:** the doc comment at `workspace2.ts:393` says implicit closes prompt for all affected workspaces regardless of unsaved changes. The code only collects workspaces with `hasUnsavedChanges`, and `explicit` is never read. Also, `launchWorkspace2` always passes `explicit: true` (line 167), so the code does not match the comment.\n\n**Documentation:**\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/launchWorkspace2.md:1-41`\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/docs/functions/launchWorkspaceGroup2.md:1-38`\n- `openmrs-esm-core/.changeset/remove-workspace-v1.md:9` (v1 APIs removed in favor of v2)\n\n**Implementation:**\n- `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts` (`launchWorkspaceGroup2`, `closeWorkspaceGroup2`, `launchWorkspace2`, `arePropsCompatible`, `promptForClosingWorkspaces`, `showClosePrompt`, `getAffectedWorkspacesInWindow`)\n- Mocks: `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-framework/mock.tsx:126-127` and `mock-jest.tsx:125-126`\n- Exports: `openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/public.ts:30-31`\n\nRanking and sources:\n1. `workspace2.ts` lines 98-321 (`launchWorkspace2` and its docs)\n2. `workspace2.ts` lines 32-63 (`launchWorkspaceGroup2`)\n3. `workspace2.ts` lines 323-339 and 398-430 (compatibility and prompt)\n4. `launchWorkspace2.md` and `launchWorkspaceGroup2.md`\n5. `action-menu-button2.component.tsx:97`\n\nI read the implementation through line 437 and did not read the rest of `workspace2.ts`. `newOpenedWorkspace` is at line 702. I did not check the `Workspace2DefinitionProps` type or `launchChildWorkspace` beyond the doc reference.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 98, \"endLine\": 321},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-core/packages/framework/esm-styleguide/src/workspaces2/workspace2.ts\", \"startLine\": 32, 